{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1302 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "428eef48953cbfbce14efc0f7ef06d79699fc81a22e18d9defc55d53cd20eea3" :edb/db-before-t 1301 :edb/db-after-t 1302 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534614 50 #inst "2026-10-12T04:47:29.390Z" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186158978 1078 #edb/ref 17592186158981 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186161862 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$, we have $\\textrm{Var}[X]=10$ and $\\textrm{Var}[Y]=12$. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\left[X-2Y\\right]$." 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186161862 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X]=10$ and $\\textrm{Var}[Y]=12.$ Find $\\textrm{Var}\\left[X-2Y\\right].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186161862 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY]=a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[X-2Y\\right]=\\left(1\\right)^2\\cdot 10+\\left(-2\\right)^2\\cdot 12 =58\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186161862 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY]=a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[X-2Y\\right]=\\left(1\\right)^2\\cdot 10+\\left(-2\\right)^2\\cdot 12 =58.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186161867 1071 "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\textrm E[X]=5$, $\\textrm E[Y]=4$\nand second raw moments $\\textrm E[X^2]=30$ and $\\textrm E[Y^2]=18$. Find the variance of $12X-11Y$." 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186161867 1071 "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\textrm E[X]=5,$ $\\textrm E[Y]=4$\nand second raw moments $\\textrm E[X^2]=30$ and $\\textrm E[Y^2]=18.$ Find the variance of  $12X-11Y.$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186161867 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY]=a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm {Var}[X]=\\textrm E[X^2]-\\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\textrm{Var}[X]$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar[X] &= E[X^{2}] - E[X]^{2} \\\\\n&= 30 - 5^{2} \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar[Y] &= E[Y^{2}] - E[Y]^{2} \\\\\n&= 18 - 4^{2} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar[12X - 11Y] &= 12^{2}Var[X] + (-11)^{2}Var[Y] \\\\\n&= 144(5) + 121(2) \\\\\n&= 962\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186161867 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY]=a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\textrm {Var}[X]=\\textrm E[X^2]-\\textrm E[X]^2.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\textrm{Var}[X]\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =30-{5}^{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =18-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[12X-11Y] & ={12}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-11)^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =144(5)+121(2) \\\\  & =962.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186161868 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$, we have $\\textrm{Var}[X]=3$ and $\\textrm{Var}[Y]=7$. Find $\\textrm{Var}[X-Y]$." 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186161868 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X]=3$ and $\\textrm{Var}[Y]=7.$ Find $\\textrm{Var}[X-Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186161868 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\textrm{Var}[X]+\\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X-Y]= 3 + 7 = 10\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186161868 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\textrm{Var}[X]+\\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X-Y]= 3 + 7 = 10.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427840 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427842 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427845 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427849 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162062 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427850 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162067 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427837 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162067 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427839 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162067 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427846 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162067 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427847 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162067 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427848 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162068 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427838 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162068 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427841 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162068 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427843 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162068 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427844 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162196 1050 420.0 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162296 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162296 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$, we have $Var[X] = 12$ and $Var[Y] = 5$. Find $Var[X - Y]$." 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186162296 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=12$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186162296 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=12+5=17.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186163250 1064 "If $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[X+Y]} = \\textrm{Var}[X]+ \\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[X-Y]} = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** When computing the variance of a *difference* of independent random variables, we *add* the variances!" 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186163250 1064 "If $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[X+Y]} = \\textrm{Var}[X]+ \\textrm{Var}[Y] ,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[X-Y]} = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y]  .\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** When computing the variance of a *difference* of independent random variables, we *add* the variances!" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186163284 1064 "We have been using the fact that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[X+Y]} = \\textrm{Var}[X]+ \\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\nUsing the property that\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]\n$$\n\nwe can show that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[aX+bY]} = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+ b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y]\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants.\n\nFor example, for two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar[4X + 3Y] &= 4^{2}Var[X] + 3^{2}Var[Y] \\\\\n&= 16Var[X] + 9Var[Y]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnce again, we need to show caution when considering a difference. For example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar[4X - 3Y] &= Var[4X + (-3)Y] \\\\\n&= 4^{2}Var[X] + (-3)^{2}Var[Y] \\\\\n&= 16Var[X] + 9Var[Y]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMore generally, if the random variables $X_1, X_2,\\ldots, X_n$, are *mutually independent*, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i X_i\\right] = \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2\\textrm{Var}[X_i]\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 false] [17592186163284 1064 "We have been using the fact that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[X+Y]} = \\textrm{Var}[X]+ \\textrm{Var}[Y]  .\n$$\n\nUsing the property that $\\textrm{Var}[aX] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X],$ we can show that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}{[aX+bY]} = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+ b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y] ,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants.\n\nFor example, for two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4X+3Y] & ={4}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =16\\text{Var}[X]+9\\text{Var}[Y]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnce again, we need to show caution when considering a difference. For example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4X-3Y] & =\\text{Var}[4X+(-3)Y] \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-3)^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =16\\text{Var}[X]+9\\text{Var}[Y].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMore generally, if the random variables $X_1, X_2,\\ldots, X_n,$ are *mutually independent*, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i X_i\\right] = \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2\\textrm{Var}[X_i].\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427753 1080 "\\frac{13}{6}" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427753 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427753 1083 #uuid "03e0da66-1167-5ea9-876f-bd4cdb5eb51d" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427754 1080 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427754 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139