1072 #uuid "126f21c0-348e-55fb-ab07-2260eac6b3ca" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427837 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =380-{18}^{2} \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =460-{21}^{2} \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[0.5X-0.3Y] & ={0.5}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-0.3)^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =0.25(56.0)+0.09(19.0) \\\\  & =15.71.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427838 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427832 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427838 1069 "q-129520" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427838 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427838 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.4$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{3}{5}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427838 1072 #uuid "18397524-502d-5cf6-a760-495d427a894e" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427838 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=0.4+\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}=1.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427839 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427834 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427839 1069 "q-109987" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427839 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427839 1071 "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.34$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.52$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.14$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[2X+7Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427839 1072 #uuid "1cad1397-85fb-5493-b4be-5ce5c5dffe60" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427839 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.34+0\\cdot 0.52+1\\cdot 0.14 \\\\  & =-0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.34+0\\cdot 0.52+1\\cdot 0.14 \\\\  & =0.48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.48-(-0.2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0.15+6\\cdot 0.6+7\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =6.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =25\\cdot 0.15+36\\cdot 0.6+49\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =37.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =37.6-{6.1}^{2} \\\\  & =0.39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X+7Y] & ={2}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{7}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =4(0.44)+49(0.39) \\\\  & =20.87.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427840 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427825 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427840 1069 "q-109964" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427840 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427840 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=16$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=14.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-2Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427840 1072 #uuid "24d4d338-4875-532e-845e-18ab4f909478" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427840 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-2Y]={(1)}^{2}\\cdot 16+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 14=72.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427841 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427827 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427841 1069 "q-129523" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427841 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427841 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427841 1072 #uuid "285af308-fbc2-5a84-995f-02e44cf826b2" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427841 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{17}{6}.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427842 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427836 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427842 1069 "q-109955" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427842 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427842 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=1$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+\\frac{2}{3}Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427842 1072 #uuid "390eb389-de35-5c0c-bca2-21dc8b96ca8a" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427842 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+\\frac{2}{3}Y]={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 1+{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 2=1.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427843 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427829 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427843 1069 "q-110356" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427843 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427843 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.5$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427843 1072 #uuid "3a356e5a-2265-58f9-b5ca-9c4228af0a92" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427843 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=0.5+2=2.5.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427844 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427835 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427844 1069 "q-110359" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427844 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427844 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=2$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427844 1072 #uuid "4eb48e05-b7d3-5766-925d-b264a050e50f" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427844 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=2+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427824 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427845 1069 "q-129527" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427845 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427845 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=36$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=4.$ Find $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X-\\frac{1}{2}Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427845 1072 #uuid "9eea5393-4f7a-57aa-9f10-8b65e7ac0b0c" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427845 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X-\\frac{1}{2}Y]={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 36+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 4=5.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427846 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427833 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427846 1069 "q-109974" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427846 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427846 1071 "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=37,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=25$\nand second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=1\\,401$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=705.$ Find the variance of  $3X+4Y.$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427846 1072 #uuid "aa8e6a54-051a-56fa-aeb3-ee00c8a84aa8" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427846 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,401-{37}^{2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =705-{25}^{2} \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X+4Y] & ={3}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{4}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =9(32)+16(80) \\\\  & =1\\,568.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427847 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427830 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427847 1069 "q-109984" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427847 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427847 1071 "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[5X-0.5Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427847 1072 #uuid "bbe4a1cf-3a7c-53c0-adbf-9f73e68e01a4" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427847 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.25+0\\cdot 0.25+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+0\\cdot 0.25+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.75-{0.25}^{2} \\\\  & =0.6875.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =10\\cdot 0.1+11\\cdot 0.7+12\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =11.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =100\\cdot 0.1+121\\cdot 0.7+144\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =123.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =123.5-{11.1}^{2} \\\\  & =0.29.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5X-0.5Y] & ={5}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-0.5)^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =25(0.6875)+0.25(0.29) \\\\  & =17.26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427848 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427828 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427848 1069 "q-129545" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427848 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427848 1071 "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{5}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{4}{5}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X-\\sqrt{5}Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427848 1072 #uuid "c320b889-ae71-5240-8135-8f57da9dfd21" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427848 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =(-1)(\\frac{1}{3})+0(\\frac{1}{3})+1(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3})+{0}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3})+{1}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{5})+2(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5})+{2}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{5}-{(\\frac{9}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X-\\sqrt{5}Y] & =(\\sqrt{3})^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-\\sqrt{5})^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+5\\cdot \\frac{4}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427849 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427826 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427849 1069 "q-109958" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427849 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427849 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=3$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=10.$ Find $\\text{Var}[6X+2Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427849 1072 #uuid "edea553d-162b-569b-a8ed-646fb2f39904" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427849 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[6X+2Y]={6}^{2}\\cdot 3+{2}^{2}\\cdot 10=148.\n$$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427850 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427831 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427850 1069 "q-109954" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427850 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427850 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.25$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.36.$ Find $\\text{Var}[3X+5Y].$" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427850 1072 #uuid "ff37b564-e7c6-5e33-b923-7014869d655b" 13194139534614 17592186045417 true] [17592186427850 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[3X+5Y]={3}^{2}\\cdot 0.25+{5}^{2}\\cdot 0.36=11.25.\n$$"